                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_435">Oxford, Oxfordshire.
                        Merton College. </orgName><p>Digby 61, fols. 1--20, contained a Merton
                        ex-libris, now missing, but recorded by Langbaine in Bodleian MS. Wood F.26,
                        p. 36, according to which 4o MS. 53 contained 'in principio' the
                        inscriptions: 'Liber Magistri Gulielmi Read Archidiaconi Roff. cuius primam
                        partem et 3am emit Oxoniæ et 2am a venerabili patro [sic] domino Tho.
                        Trillek Episcopo Roff. oretis igitur pro singulis supradictis'; and 'Liber
                        domus de Merton Oxon' in Libraria communi eiusdem et ad usum communem
                        Magistrorum et sociorum ibidem studentium catenandus ex dono venerabilis
                        patris domini Willelmi 3i episcopi Cicestr' Oretis igitur pro eodem et
                        benefactoribus'.</p></provenance>
